INSERT INTO concern VALUES('collapse','Collapse','A space reduced to its critical cells: an acyclic matching pairs each cell that cancels with a face one dimension down, and the cells that no pair holds stay. A complex states the faces of each cell with their incidence, and a scheme states the class of each cell. The Morse crate checks a scheme on the cells a caller gives and follows the gradient past them up to a budget. A walk past its budget is refused, never cut short. The reduct keeps the critical cells with the boundary that the gradient paths give, and a sheaf reduces onto them where each matched map is invertible. Completion''s critical pairs are the critical cells of Brown''s collapsing scheme on the bar complex of a rule block.','theory-discrete-morse::Complex','#5507');
INSERT INTO concern VALUES('fork','Fork','Work split across the driver''s one pool: the fork crate states the trait and its serial reference, and every consumer forks through it.','core-fork::Fork','#1250');
INSERT INTO concern VALUES('measure','Measure','A value that a cell carries in an ordered algebra and that an analysis propagates: a grade, a weight, a cost or a distance. An ordered semiring states the carrier, the operations and the order. The law checker decides the semiring''s laws on every tuple of a finite carrier, or on the elements an infinite one generates, and names a counterexample for each broken law. An operation past the represented elements answers undecided, never a guess.','theory-ordered-algebras::OrderedSemiring','#5308');
INSERT INTO concern VALUES('nominal','Nominal','Names with identity, order, freshness and support, and the lifecycle a unit runs over them. A register store holds each name at most once, and a transfer retains, allocates or erases one. A lifecycle is a word or a tree over the alphabet of allocations, uses and releases, and a nominal automaton with name allocation and deallocation accepts it or not. Name dropping closes its language under renaming. Literal membership is decided; emptiness, inclusion and determinization belong to the classical back end, deferred until a unit needs one.',NULL,'#4181');
INSERT INTO concern VALUES('oracle','Oracle','A decision the kernel asks of a module that answers with evidence the kernel checks. A metaprogram stands as one: `Eq.generic`''s derived core is judged and readmitted as if written, so the derivation itself is never trusted. A foreign semantics stands as one: a Rust function''s THIR, written as data, has each weakest precondition computed by a fold the kernel replays, so only the data''s fidelity to rustc is trusted (`rust-semantics-thir`). A trusted kernel''s receipt stands as one: a recorded verdict is believed on a signature the kernel verifies, under the operator''s policy, so only the signer is trusted, and `--recheck` re-derives every verdict (`attested-verdict-cache`). An evaluator stands as one: the emitter meets an endpoint pair, closed or open, for the checker, and the kernel converts the pair by its own evaluation, so no engine decision reaches the trusted base for it (`native-conversion`). Under `--admit native-conversion` the kernel takes a closed pair''s answer instead, so the emitter is trusted for that run alone, and the run says so.',NULL,'#313');
INSERT INTO concern VALUES('sharing','Sharing','A descent datum: positions, a coverage of which positions share, a compatibility, a gluing done once, and a certificate the kernel replays. A cell''s per-hole occurrence count is the size of one such coverage: the positions of its right side that share the subterm its left side matched at the hole. An effect theory''s law shares requests: the requests a scope''s subject makes in a run its left side covers, nothing but returns between them, are glued into its right side''s fewer, the law''s orientation the certificate the kernel replays with the theory and the handler''s check as a model the reason the gluing changes no answer. A kernel memo key names a plain definition''s reference by its declared type and body, not its admission position, so two environments that admitted the same declarations in another order build one key for one question. Sharing points are local or global: a location-addressable heap shares a cell by its index, a wrapping indirection inside one world, and the content-addressable store shares a chunk by its digest, a boundary any world dereferences; what a duplication costs is the boundary and alias classification''s to say. A checkpoint is local: a function of its own source and of the sources that source reaches. A cover of a spectrum is a unimodular sequence with its coefficients, and inclusion of opens is membership in a radical ideal, so a coverage is an equation in the algebra and never a set the kernel walks. A result over a support restricts to a sub-support by localising its key.',NULL,'#2291');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('bisimulation','built','the nodes of a plan graph that its root reaches','a class of nodes that unfold alike, a sum, a product, a meet and a join read with their operands as a multiset','equal labels, and for each class an equal count of operands in it at each position, or in all positions for an unordered label','one class for each unfolding, and the key a digest of the classes numbered from the root','none: the key feeds no judgement, and the canonical bytes of a plan stay the identity that the cache and the checker read');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('cell-holes','built','a cell''s right-side occurrences of one hole','the subterm its left side matched at the hole','one match per hole, the same subterm at each occurrence','the match bound once and written at each occurrence','none: the count is the hole''s Lipschitz constant, which the derivation reports and refuses nowhere');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('checked-results','built','the settled obligations of an exact-reals run, across runs and plans','the canonical bytes of the plan that the obligation''s node roots, with its demand','byte equality of the key, the stored certificate moved to the positions of the plan that asks','one certificate held per key, read by every run that asks the same judgement of the same subterm','the checker''s replay of the moved certificate against the plan that asks, before the machine uses it');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('congruence-closure','built','the terms that an e-graph holds, each a place of a Lawvere theory''s table','a class of terms that the input equations and congruence join','two nodes of one head whose arguments lie in one class lie in one class','one class for each set of equal terms, its parents kept once for each signature and repaired once for each rebuild','the explanation of each equality: a path of the proof forest whose input steps are instances of the equations and whose congruence steps cite the proofs of their arguments, replayed against the table and the equations alone');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('content-chunks','built','a value''s subtrees at its boundary constructors','the chunk digest over canonical bytes','deep equality of the chunk''s value','one chunk stored per digest, read by every pointer to it, in any world','the manifest''s boundary and alias classification and the deep-equality round trip');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('courant-leroy','built','comparison subproblems ordered by the wait graph','the memo''s keys with support edges','permutation equivalence of reduction choices: the trace monoid','one channel per key, one process per pair','the conversion trace');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('cover-derivation','built','the leaves of a match''s decision tree','the cover derivation: each split one column''s cases, each composition a split under a branch','each data split''s constructors and loops as the admitted family lists them, and each step meeting its own node of the tree','the decision tree, which runs the arm each leaf names','the kernel''s replay of the derivation against the tree at the definition''s admission');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('cover-gluing','built','the members of a cover, each a cell of a graded poset with a section on its stalk','the least cells above two members, read from the meet of their stars','the two restrictions equal at each entry of each least cell of the overlap','one section on every cell above a member, each cell read from the first member below it','none: the sheaves crate decides the gluing by computation outside the trusted base, and the kernel replays nothing of it');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('effect-laws','built','the requests a scope''s subject makes in one run','an instance of a law''s oriented left side','nothing but returns between the requests, each payload checked at its type','the right side''s fewer requests, each dropped request replaced by returning its reply','the law''s orientation, replayed by the kernel with the theory; the handler''s check as a model is why the gluing changes no answer');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('exact-records','built','the one-level records an arena holds: a tag, a payload and the children''s ids','exact syntactic identity of the record','equality of every field, confirmed by comparison and never by a hash','one id per record, read wherever the record recurs','none: an id decides syntactic identity and nothing more, computed rather than asserted, so this is not hash-consing');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('hash-consing','banned','every subterm','syntactic identity','equality','a table','none: the degenerate coverage, asserted rather than computed');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('heap-reuse','built','a run''s heap cells','the references to one cell by its index, counted','one value per index, an index never recycled','one cell read through every reference; a cell whose count is one rebuilt in place by the constructor its match pairs with','none: the reference count, local to the run and never replayed');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('incremental-memo','built','the decomposition''s parts, across edits','per-part data','interface agreement','the assembly','the memo''s keys');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('record-leaves','built','a sorted record sequence''s runs, cut between records','the node hash over a leaf''s canonical encoding','equal runs cut alike, a boundary a function of the records alone','one node per hash in the block store, read by every root whose leaves reach it','none: a membership, absence or range proof checked against the root shows what a root commits, never that a record is valid');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('sharing-equality','built','the nodes two readings reach, related by the queries a comparison poses','a class of nodes the queries join, with the first node it was built from','each member agrees with its class''s first node in former and payload, their children queried pairwise, and a parent''s class closes before its child''s','one class for each node, the two readings equal when their roots share one','none: the comparison decides whether the tier meets a pair, and the kernel converts a met pair by its own evaluation');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('spinal','built','occurrences under a binder','the spine, each maximal rib a leg','the spinal calculus''s two permutation quotients','a leg evaluated once per configuration','the property against the copying stance, and the conversion trace a traced verdict records');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('subterm-table','built','every subterm of an exported artifact','structural equality, computed bottom-up by the writer','equality of tag, child indices and inline payload','one table entry, referenced by every parent','the reader''s re-encode-compare: the writer is untrusted and feeds no judgement, so this is not hash-consing');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('superposition','built','members of a family indexed by guard points','the schema','agreement away from the guarded points, a member a guard vector','one schema check, rows by exact identity','the schema and its rows');
INSERT INTO descent VALUES('useful-sharing','built','a shared domain value''s occurrences in a read-back term','the domain value and the binders open where it stands','one run''s mode, definitions and written hole, which fix what the value reads back to','one core node built once and referenced at every occurrence','none: the kernel checks the read-back term, and two domain nodes of equal content stay two core nodes, so this is not hash-consing');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-cellular-sheaves','reduce','implements',NULL,'`Oriented` and `Sheaf::reduce`: a sheaf''s poset as a complex over the integers for the greedy matching, and the cochains reduced along the walk of each critical cell where each matched map is invertible.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-coherent-resolutions','basis','implements',NULL,'`Basis`: the confluences and the critical triples of a convergent cell system as one complex, a triple''s faces the confluences in the boundary of its 4-cell, and a pair only where the confluence occurs there once, at the root and with no context; the reduction is its scheme, and its composites are homotopies and 4-cells.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-coherent-resolutions','completion','implements',NULL,'`PairScheme`, `PairClass`, `PairJoining::resume_with` and `scheduled_confluence_batches`: each critical pair classed before the joining decides it, each root branching joined once, and the join of a composite pair skipped as redundant, its witness kept.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-coherent-resolutions','lawvere','implements',NULL,'The bar complex of a first-order block''s Lawvere theory as a complex: the first, inner and last faces of a cell, equal faces summed, and a cell inside when it is proper, composable and in normal form.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-coherent-resolutions','lawvere::brown','implements',NULL,'Brown''s collapsing scheme on that bar complex as a `Scheme`: each cell read from the left along the leftmost innermost redex, and classed redundant, collapsible or essential with its partner.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-coherent-resolutions','triple','implements',NULL,'`critical_triples` and `CriticalTriple`: the generating cells of dimension four, three steps on one peak that the overlaps of their left-hand sides connect, each counted once over the orders of its steps.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-deep-inference','reduction','implements',NULL,'`TemplateReduction` and `TemplateFold`: a family of certificates collapsed onto the template of its `GuardedForm`, each member to its row, the guard of the arm that it holds at each entry, read from its peak with no copy of a body, and each row included back as its instance, held as its peak and its join; a tracelet instance over the carrier''s skeleton, and a staging instance as the template''s sides with the arms in place; a family of families collapsed onto one template of templates, each member''s row with its template''s row there.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-discrete-morse','abelian','implements',NULL,'`Abelian` and `Chain`: a scheme''s composites read as integer chains, the linear shadow of the equivalence, whose collapse of each critical boundary is the Morse boundary of the reduct.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-discrete-morse','collapse','defines',NULL,'`Scheme` and `collapse`: the class of each cell, and the check of a scheme as an acyclic matching that keeps the critical cells and counts each fault.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-discrete-morse','complex','defines',NULL,'`Complex`, `Incidence` and `Complex::pairing`: the faces of a cell one dimension down, each with its incidence, whether a cell lies in the complex, and whether a face can pair with a cell.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-discrete-morse','equivalence','defines',NULL,'`Composites`, `Equivalence`, `equivalence` and `Bound`: a complex equivalent to its reduct on its own composites, the collapse sending each redundant cell to its partner''s definition in gradient order and each partner to an identity, the inclusion conjugating each critical cell by the witnesses of its removed faces.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-discrete-morse','greedy','implements',NULL,'`greedy`: a matching built in list order, each pair kept only when no gradient path runs back from the upper cell to the lower one.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-discrete-morse','matching','implements',NULL,'`Matching` and `Matched`: a matching that the greedy search builds or that a caller states pair by pair, a Tietze move stating one pair, read as a scheme over any complex whose faces, pairing condition and composites it reads unchanged.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-discrete-morse','poset','implements',NULL,'A `GradedPoset` as a complex: the faces of a cell are the cells of its boundary one rank down, each with the incidence one.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-discrete-morse','reduct','defines',NULL,'`reduct` and `Reduct`: the critical cells by rank and then by place, the Morse boundary of each summed along its gradient paths, and the walk of each.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-discrete-morse','reduction','defines',NULL,'`Reduction` and `Then`: a collapse with its inclusion and the witness of each inverse law, and two in sequence, the collapses composed, the inclusions composed in reverse order and the witnesses whiskered.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-discrete-morse','sum','defines',NULL,'`Sum` and `Summand`: reductions of one type side by side as one reduction, each cell, composite and witness with its part, and each map read in that part.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-exact-reals','graph','implements',NULL,'`PlanGraph::core`: a plan graph as a complex of dimension one, each ranked node with operands matched with the edge to its first operand one rank down, so the critical nodes are the recursive core and an acyclic plan has none.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('collapse','theory-graded-posets','traversal','implements',NULL,'`GradedPoset::traverse`, `Traversal` and `Key`: Kessler''s traversal of a molecule, and its faces written as places in traversal order, so the complex of a collapse is named up to isomorphism.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('fork','core-fork','','defines',NULL,'The `Fork` trait and `Serial`, the pool of one that a consumer runs on alone.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('fork','kernel-core','check','consumes',NULL,'`drain_forked`: a declaration''s last drain of 64 obligations or more, checked apart in runs, one for each worker of the driver''s fork, and folded in the serial order.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('fork','kernel-core','fork','defines',NULL,'`ObligationFork` and `Job`: the object-safe seam a judgement carries. The kernel sits below the core crates, so it states the seam itself, and the driver''s pool implements it.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('fork','runtime-emitter','cut','consumes',NULL,'`evaluate_scheduled_on`: each writer a scheduled program spawns started on the caller''s fork, each read waiting for its writer.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('fork','surface-dispatcher','pool','implements',NULL,'`Pool` and `Pooled`, the driver-held pool that every consumer forks on. `Pool` is the kernel''s `ObligationFork` too.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('fork','surface-dispatcher','pool::recording','implements',NULL,'`ActivityFork`: the pool''s recording fork, each job run as the pool runs it between a start mark and an end mark on the ring of its thread.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('fork','surface-dispatcher','verdicts','consumes',NULL,'`install_obligation_fork`: the fork that each kernel check of a process drains its obligations through, carried into each readmission''s recall.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('fork','surface-session','forms','consumes',NULL,'`mold_runs`: a revision''s changed forms molded on the session''s pool, one molder per worker.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('fork','surface-session','session','consumes',NULL,'`Session::trial_unit`: a trial''s candidates judged on the session''s pool, each result in its own slot.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('fork','workflow-lane-budget','github','implements',NULL,'`read_all`: a report''s `gh` reads split across scoped threads of its own, outside the driver''s pool.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('measure','core-checker-base','judgement::access','consumes',NULL,'The hold rule and `linear_read`: the uses on a held value added in the usage semiring, and the sum admitted only at or below the grade''s bound.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('measure','core-term','effect::capability','implements',NULL,'`CapabilityGrade::usage`: a capability''s grade as its bound in the usage semiring, many when durable and one when consumable.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('measure','core-term','memory','implements',NULL,'`HoldGrade::usage`: a hold''s grade as its bound in the usage semiring, many at grade ω and one at grade one.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('measure','surface-corpus','distribution','consumes',NULL,'`distributed`: each path of a declaration''s runs weighed `2^-n` for the `n` bits its draws take, summed by outcome into one `Distribution`, whose canonical form a `distributes` expectation compares.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('measure','surface-dispatcher','cells::fusion','consumes',NULL,'The census''s fusion rows: the distance of each fusion cell''s two steps and each hole''s count composed in the Lawvere quantale, and compared with the fused cell''s own counts.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('measure','theory-exact-reals','dyadic','implements',NULL,'`Dyadic::simplest`: the dyadic of least mantissa width strictly inside an open interval, the one point of the coarsest grid that meets it, found in time linear in the ends'' bits.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('measure','theory-ordered-algebras','amplitude','implements',NULL,'`Amplitudes` and `RealAmplitudes`: the exact amplitudes `ℤ[1/√2, i]` and their real subring `ℤ[1/√2]` as commutative rings under the discrete order, each element at its least scale.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('measure','theory-ordered-algebras','instance','implements',NULL,'`Tropical` and `Lawvere`: the max-plus semiring and the Lawvere quantale of distances, over exact dyadics.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('measure','theory-ordered-algebras','law','defines',NULL,'`check` and `check_ring`: the sixteen laws, and the two that a commutative ring adds, decided on a carrier, each broken law named with its counterexample.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('measure','theory-ordered-algebras','signature','defines',NULL,'`OrderedSemiring` and `CommutativeRing`: the carrier, the operations and the order that every measure states, and the negation of a ring.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('measure','theory-ordered-algebras','usage','defines',NULL,'`Usage` and `Usages`: the usage semiring {0, 1, ω}, its addition, its multiplication and its order, and its instance on the whole carrier, whose laws the suite `tests::laws` decides.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('measure','theory-probability','distribution','implements',NULL,'`Distribution`: exact positive weights in the rationals over a finite support, multiplied along the Kleisli extension and the product, summed where points merge, and divided by the weight of an event.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('measure','theory-probability','junction','consumes',NULL,'`JunctionTree::calibrate`: sum-product over any ordered semiring, each message a product of tables marginalised by the semiring''s sum, so probability gives the marginals and max-times the greatest weight.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('measure','theory-probability','semiring','implements',NULL,'`Probability` and `MaxTimes`: the probability and the max-times semirings over the non-negative rationals, each passing the sixteen laws on a generated carrier.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('nominal','theory-coherent-resolutions','rewrite','implements',NULL,'A firing of a cell with wires: each wire takes a name apart from the term it enters, primed until the term does not hold it, so a wire is a scoped name minted at its introduction.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('nominal','theory-nominal-automata','handle','defines',NULL,'`Store`: a partial injective map from registers to caller-owned names, read for `Freshness`, and the `Transfer`s that retain, allocate or erase a name.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('nominal','theory-nominal-automata','letter','defines',NULL,'`Letter`: the alphabet a lifecycle is a word over, a free use, an allocation, a release and an immediate release.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('nominal','theory-nominal-automata','nda','defines',NULL,'`Nda` and `name_dropping`: the word automaton with name deallocation, its literal membership, and the erasure that closes its language under renaming.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('nominal','theory-nominal-automata','rnta','defines',NULL,'`Rnta` and `Term`: the tree automaton with name allocation, and the term arena whose free names follow lexical scope.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('nominal','theory-probability','joint','implements',NULL,'`Distribution::independent` and `Independence`: a joint whose weight at each pair is the product of its marginal weights, the probabilistic form of the separation of supports, or the first pair where it is not.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('nominal','theory-shapes','boundary','consumes',NULL,'`Boundary`: a shape''s carrier as a `Store` of its names in name order, a face a set of names retained and an inclusion a release of the names its source lacks.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','core-checker-base','tier','defines',NULL,'The `EndpointTier` trait a driver hands a context: an endpoint pair, closed or open over its context, met before the machine, its side recorded as the one decision `Evaluate`, or `Admitted` for a closed pair under the admission policy.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','core-checker-base','ua::strata','defines',NULL,'The `StratumStore` trait a driver hands a context: a stored stratum believed on its receipt, replayed against its catalogue before it is read, and certified afresh when it does not replay.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','kernel-core','admitted','defines',NULL,'The admission policy: under `NativeConversion` a closed pair''s `Admitted` side taken without deriving it, the emitter trusted for that run; under `Derive` converted as an `Evaluate` side is.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','kernel-core','element_identity','consumes',NULL,'The `here` rule''s `Evaluate` side: both sides, closed or open, converted by `convert_unfolding` within the replay''s budget, a decline refused; an `Admitted` side taken or converted as the admission policy says.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','kernel-core','levels','consumes',NULL,'The level context: the potential maintenance proposes a model of a declaration''s difference constraints, and the landmark poset validates the model before it admits.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','kernel-core','verdict','defines',NULL,'The trusted receipt: a recorded verdict believed on a signature the kernel verifies, under the operator''s policy.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','kernel-strata','level','implements',NULL,'The universe-level algebra in its always-canonical form.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','kernel-strata','order','implements',NULL,'The order oracle, answering with evidence a validator recomputes.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','surface-dispatcher','tier','implements',NULL,'`Emitted`: both sides of a pair run on the emitter, each free variable an accumulator, and read back, a run stepping a native operation or spending its fuel left to the machine.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-coherent-resolutions','basis','implements',NULL,'`Composites::replays` for `Basis`: the witness of a removed confluence checked and never trusted. Each fill names a cut of a built boundary, its confluence stands at the move, the homotopy reached runs move by move, and it is the replacement.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-coherent-resolutions','completion','implements',NULL,'`CompositePair::replay`: a skipped pair''s witness checked and never trusted. Both legs fire at the peak, the redex stands strictly below the seam and its cell replays there with the witness''s substitution, and a forged witness is refused by name.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-coherent-resolutions','rewrite','implements',NULL,'`replay_at`: a recorded step checked and never trusted. Its substitution instantiates the cell''s left side, the instance is compared with the command at the step''s position, a forged substitution is refused by name, and the step contracts.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-computads','term::composite','implements',NULL,'`CompositeCriterion`: the composite class of a critical pair, answered with the redex below its seam as evidence that `CompositePair::replay` checks.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-deep-inference','reduction','implements',NULL,'`TemplateReduction::replay` and `TemplateFold::replay`: the folds checked and never trusted. Each member''s row gives an instance, the instance gives the row back, and the instance equals the member, as the guarded form holds it in place; each carrier equals the instance of its own row in the template of templates; each failure refused by name.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-discrete-morse','equivalence','implements',NULL,'`Equivalence::replay`: the definitions of a matching checked and never trusted. The matching passes the collapse check, each witness closes, the replacements run in gradient order and `φ ∘ ι` gives each critical cell back, each failure refused by name.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-discrete-morse','reduction','implements',NULL,'`Then::replay`: two reductions checked as one. Each replays, the first target is the second source, `φ ∘ ι` gives each target cell back or its retraction closes, and each section closes, each failure refused by name. The first collapse of each seam cell is read once and kept, and the round trip and the section of a cell share one inclusion.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-discrete-morse','sum','implements',NULL,'`Sum::replay`: each part checked in part order, each refusal named with its part.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-e-graphs','egraph::explain','implements',NULL,'`Explanation::replay`: an e-graph''s explanation checked and never trusted. Each input step is its equation at its values, each congruence step joins two nodes of one head whose arguments earlier proofs join, the last proof joins the two terms asked, and each forged step is refused by name.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-exact-reals','approx','implements',NULL,'Dual approximation: an enclosure of each real node and a positive and a negative approximant of each open node, each sound on its own, the computed half of a judgement whose certificate the checker replays.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-exact-reals','bisection','implements',NULL,'The search of a bounded quantifier: pieces of its domain visited breadth first, each enclosed under a hypothesis on the variable, a witness, a cover, a counterexample or a refutation that the checker replays, and a search past its budget never a falsehood.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-exact-reals','cache','implements',NULL,'The checked-result cache: evidence and never a verdict, each hit replayed in the checker against the plan that asks, an entry that does not replay dropped and refused by name.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-exact-reals','certificate','implements',NULL,'The certificate checker: a list of primitive steps replayed with exact dyadic arithmetic and comparison alone, a hypothesis on a bound variable discharged by a witness or a cover of the domain, each malformed step refused by name and the work bounded by quotas, the replayed half of a judgement whose approximants are computed.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-exact-reals','dovetail','implements',NULL,'The dovetailing scheduler: typed obligations run in bounded quanta, in a fixed order and within a budget, each one certified by a certificate that the checker replays or stopped for a stated reason, and none of its outcomes read as false.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-exact-reals','interval','implements',NULL,'Outward-rounded interval approximants: an enclosure that a refinement step reads to choose its next split, never evidence that a comparison holds, so the certificate checker of a later stage replays the exact dyadic comparisons and nothing of the interval code.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-exact-reals','schema','implements',NULL,'`Split`: the point of each split of the producer, the midpoint or the dyadic of least width, which the checker admits at any point inside the enclosure, so the policy changes the certificates and never what they prove.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('oracle','theory-exact-reals','semidecision','implements',NULL,'The producer of certificates: one certificate step for each unit of work on an obligation, outside the checker, a refusal of the producer a suspension of the obligation and never a falsehood.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','core-checker','staging','consumes','exact-records','The merge: each worker''s classifiers and terms interned into the program''s arena in source order, a held one found and compared, only a miss appended.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','core-checker-bridge','bridge','consumes','incremental-memo','`formation_key` and `formed`: a patched type''s formation keyed by the content of its fixed values and of each round of meets in the content table, so equal brackets at two core nodes cross one formation.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','core-checker-bridge','template','implements','superposition','Guarded families of staging equations: one template drafted and priced for a family of one producer''s equations, ordinary replay the authority.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','core-incremental','','implements','incremental-memo','Incremental checking: validated resume and content-addressed checkpoints.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','core-nbe','duplicate','implements','spinal','Spinal atomic duplication, admitted under the testing stance on its agreement with the copying stance.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','core-nbe','eval','implements','spinal','The machine''s leg sharing: a leg''s first weak head in one configuration remembered, and taken by every later occurrence read in it.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','core-nbe','machine','implements','courant-leroy','The lazy concurrent convertibility search and its memo, its channels keyed per body and, under the spinal granularity, per prefix of a spine.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','core-nbe','readback','implements','useful-sharing','Readback''s table for one run: a shared domain value read once at each binder depth, so the normal form keeps the sharing the domain held.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','core-nbe','resharing','implements','courant-leroy','The memo''s resharing of a comparison already decided.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','core-nbe','traced','implements','spinal','The spinal stance on the certifying path: a root evaluated through its own duplicate, its shared legs handed to the machine, its conversions recorded for replay.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','core-nbe-base','overlay','implements','spinal','The overlay a spinal leg''s evaluation is shared through.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','core-term','handler::subject','implements','effect-laws','A theory''s laws as rewrites of a scope''s subject: a run of requests a law''s left side covers glued into its right side''s fewer before the scope runs.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','core-term','syntax::shared','implements','sharing-equality','The blind check: two readings compared as the graphs they are shared as, in time linear in the nodes they reach.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','kernel-check-memo','','implements','incremental-memo','The check-memo seam a checker consults.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','kernel-conversion-trace','','defines','courant-leroy','The conversion-decision seam: the trace an engine emits for a comparison it decided once, which the kernel replays without search.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','kernel-core','admission','implements','superposition','Guarded-superposition admission: one schema check for a family of members.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','kernel-core','admission::content','implements','exact-records','The consumer-owned arena a binding''s rows look their records up in, an id deciding syntactic identity with no hash premise.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','kernel-core','check::cover','implements','cover-derivation','The replay of each match''s derivation at its definition''s admission: every data split re-derives its family''s constructors and loops and meets its own data case, so the tree''s branch count follows from the derivation.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','kernel-core','encoding','implements','incremental-memo','The memo key, naming a plain definition''s reference by its content, over a content table that names each node once for its environment''s life.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','kernel-core','replay','implements','spinal','The replay''s weak-head reduction under an environment: the value a binder stands for held once in a cell for every occurrence and closed once at the unload, admitted on its agreement with the substituting reduction.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','kernel-core','support','implements','incremental-memo','The support of one node check. It is the complete input that a memo key names. Equal supports force equal answers. With the judgement''s parameters beside it, the support keys the content outcomes that an environment keeps across its admissions.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','kernel-core','verdict','implements','incremental-memo','The verdict key, chaining the kernel''s build and each admitted declaration, read by every later run over the same prefix.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','kernel-term','decode','consumes','subterm-table','The reader''s re-encode-compare: an artifact accepted only when the maximal-sharing encoder reproduces its bytes.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','kernel-term','encode','implements','subterm-table','The writer''s subterm table: nodes interned bottom-up by their entry bytes, two structurally equal subterms one entry across declarations.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','kernel-term','stage','implements','exact-records','The staging arena: classifiers and terms interned by exact syntactic equality, a held descriptor found by hash and confirmed by comparison.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','kernel-term','support','implements','incremental-memo','The support column every node carries: the free indices a memo key reads off a node without walking its term.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','runtime-emitter','crossing','consumes','content-chunks','`crossing::commit`: a store''s value written to the value plane however the store shares it, a subtree written twice stored once by content; `crossing::deref` lays a tree.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','runtime-emitter','lower','implements','heap-reuse','The reuse token: a scrutinee whose fields an arm took is rebuilt in place by the constructor the ownership reading pairs with it.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','runtime-emitter','world','consumes','content-chunks','A migration''s captures and answer crossing by content through a chunk store of that crossing alone; `arrive` runs one another host shipped here.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','runtime-net','chunks','consumes','content-chunks','The chunk wire: a fetch naming the values its asker holds carries only the chunks their closures lack, so a chunk two sends share crosses once.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','storage-artifact','record::value','implements','content-chunks','A kernel artifact on the value plane: each declaration segment''s constructor holds the one before it, so an edit to a declaration shares every chunk before it, across edits and across the packages one store holds.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','storage-chunker','typed','implements','content-chunks','The typed scanner: a value''s chunk cut where a residue divides kappa or the cap fires, at a boundary constructor''s exit.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','storage-records','','implements','record-leaves','The keyed plane''s tree: a sorted record sequence cut into leaves at content-defined boundaries, each node stored once by its hash.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','storage-values','commit','defines','content-chunks','`cam_commit`: a value cut at its boundary constructors into chunks named by digest, the boundary and alias classification deciding where a cut falls.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','surface-dispatcher','cells::fusion','consumes','cell-holes','The census''s fusion rows: each hole''s count, the size of its coverage, read from the two cells'' metadata and glued along the derivation of a composition overlap.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','surface-dispatcher','stored','consumes','content-chunks','`StoreAccount`: the in-degree of each chunk among the closures of the stored values, the size of the coverage of the values that hold it whole, read from the value plane and never changed.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','surface-dispatcher','strata','consumes','incremental-memo','The stratum store a driver installs: a certified stratum committed under its bound, degree and theory build, and replayed by every later process that names that key.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','surface-dispatcher','verdicts','consumes','incremental-memo','The verdict cache a driver installs: each readmission recalls the receipt its verdict key names, and one that crossed whole keeps the kernel''s.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','surface-evaluate','evaluate::worlds','consumes','content-chunks','A migration''s captures fetched by the host that runs it, skipping each it holds whole and naming every value it holds, so a value it made itself crosses back to it as nothing.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','surface-lowering-base','table','implements','incremental-memo','A suspended lowering''s per-node cells, shared behind one `Arc` with every lowering resumed from it, a cell copied only when written.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','surface-parser','meld','implements','incremental-memo','The resumable melder: a checkpoint at a declaration boundary, resumed to parse what follows as a fresh parse would.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','surface-session','session','consumes','incremental-memo','Each revision offered to the incremental checker, which adopts every checkpoint that still answers and persists the set.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','theory-cell-complexes','sequent','consumes','cell-holes','A cell''s per-hole contractum use: how many times a step writes the subterm its left side matched at each hole, the size of that hole''s coverage.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','theory-cellular-sheaves','sheaf','defines','cover-gluing','`Sheaf::glue`: the sections of a cover compared at the least cells above each two members, each pair that differs named with that cell and its first entry, or the sections glued to one section on every cell above a member.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','theory-deep-inference','reduction','implements','superposition','`TemplateFold`: one template of templates for a family of families, the carriers of its member templates borrowed and folded into it where that pays.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','theory-deep-inference','template','implements','superposition','Guarded templates: one certificate for a family firing the same cells at the same positions, an arm per distinct member subterm, each arm''s inheritance check memoized, the members held by the family or borrowed.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','theory-e-graphs','egraph','implements','congruence-closure','`EGraph`: one class for each set of terms that the equations and congruence join, over the places of a Lawvere theory''s table, its parents kept once for each signature and repaired once for each rebuild.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','theory-exact-reals','cache','implements','checked-results','The checked-result cache: one certificate for each subterm and demand, keyed by the canonical bytes of the plan that the subterm roots, so two plans that hold the subterm share it.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','theory-exact-reals','codec','consumes','subterm-table','The plan reader''s re-encode-compare: plan bytes accepted only when the canonical walk writes them again, so a duplicate node, a dead node or another order is refused.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','theory-exact-reals','minimal','implements','bisimulation','`PlanGraph::minimal`: the coarsest partition stable under the operand counts, then the classes numbered from the root and digested into the key, so two plans that unfold alike share one key.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','theory-exact-reals','plan','implements','subterm-table','The canonical walk: a plan''s nodes interned bottom-up by their entry bytes, two structurally equal subterms one node and a shared subterm one edge.');
INSERT INTO site VALUES('sharing','theory-probability','glue','implements','cover-gluing','`Family::glue`: local tables compared on each overlap by marginalisation in the semiring, each entry that differs named with both weights, or the shared table on each overlap.');
